{title: You Knit Me Together}
{subtitle: Psalm 139}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 76}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [F/A] | [Gm] |
| [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]Lord, you have searched me and [F/A]known me
[Gm]You know when I sit [Eb]down and when I [Bb]rise
You discern my thoughts [F/A]from far away
[Gm]Before a word is on my [Eb]tongue
You know it altogeth[Bb]er
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
You knit me togeth[F]er in my mother's [Gm]womb
I am fear[Eb]fully and wonderfully [Bb]made
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Where shall I [F]go from your Spir[Gm]it [Eb]
[Bb]Where shall I flee from your [F/A]presence
[Gm]If I ascend to heav[Eb]en, you [Bb]are there
If I make my bed in [Gm]the depths, you are [Eb]there
[Gm]Even the darkness is [Eb]not dark to [Bb]you
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{comment: Instrumental}
| [Bb] | [F] | [Gm] | [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Bb]Search me, O [F]God, and all my [Gm]heart [Eb]
{end_of_verse}
